101: ## 📦 Standalone Executable & Windows Installer (.msi)
102: 
103: ### Running the Standalone Executable
104: You do **not** need Python installed to run the compiled application:
105: * Location: `dist\FileSentinel.exe`
106: * Double-click `FileSentinel.exe` to launch the native desktop application immediately.
107: * It embeds the dashboard, assets, and watchdog engine into a single portable binary.
108: 
109: ### Installing via Windows Installer (.msi)
110: * Location: `dist\FileSentinel-Setup.msi`
111: * Double-click `FileSentinel-Setup.msi` to run the standard Windows installation wizard.
112: * Installs `FileSentinel` to `C:\Program Files\FileSentinel`.
113: * Automatically creates Desktop and Start Menu shortcuts.
114: * Can be uninstalled cleanly at any time through Windows **Settings > Apps > Installed apps** or **Control Panel**.
115: 
116: ### Building `.exe` and `.msi` from Source
117: To rebuild both binaries at any time, run the automated PowerShell script:
118: ```powershell
119: powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\build_all.ps1
120: ```
121: This script handles dependency verification, PyInstaller frozen bundling, portable WiX Toolset setup, and `.msi` compilation.
